            "splits": "A trunk a metre across, as the blocks are, is 0.785 m² of wood in section. It splits by halves along its grain, as rails are split; halved six times it gives 64 billets of about 0.012 m², some 11 cm square, each dressed to the 8 to 10 cm round of an outrigger's booms, mast and spars. Every row, whatever its length, splits into poles as long as it is"
